SCHEMA BROWSER NEW GET API – CODE REVIEW EXPLANATION

1. FIRST EXPLAIN WHAT WE ARE DOING

The requirement is to create a new GET API in Schema Browser to retrieve active Field Map configuration records from Oracle.

The query was provided by Mahesh.

The API retrieves:

1. FIELD_MAP_SK
2. TABLE_PHYSICAL_NAME
3. FINAL_QUERY
4. RUN_FREQUENCY

from:

C167969RPC.OM_CATALOGUE_FIELD_MAP_LKP

where:

IS_CURRENT_FLAG = 'Y'

and the records are ordered by:

DWH_CREATED_TIMESTAMP

The API returns the records as JSON.

We are using the existing Schema Browser Oracle datasource and Spring JdbcTemplate. We are not creating a new database connection.

Overall flow:

Client
   ↓
FieldMapConfigController
   ↓
FieldMapConfigService
   ↓
JdbcTemplate
   ↓
Oracle Database
   ↓
ResultSet
   ↓
FieldMapConfigResponse
   ↓
JSON Response


==================================================
2. FIRST OPEN: FieldMapConfigController.java
==================================================

I will start with the controller because this is where the HTTP request enters the application.

package com.citihawk.schemabrowser.controller;

This class is under the existing Schema Browser controller package.


IMPORTS:

import com.citihawk.schemabrowser.model.schemabrowser.FieldMapConfigResponse;
import com.citihawk.schemabrowser.service.FieldMapConfigService;

FieldMapConfigService contains the database retrieval logic.

FieldMapConfigResponse represents the response that will be returned as JSON.


@RestController

This tells Spring that this class exposes REST endpoints.

