        LoggerFactory.getLogger(FieldMapConfigController.class);

This logger is used to write execution information into the application logs.


@Autowired
private FieldMapConfigService fieldMapConfigService;

Spring injects the FieldMapConfigService here.

We keep the database logic inside the service instead of putting it directly inside the controller.

This separates the API layer from the business/database layer.


